# Integration test binaries that must not run concurrently.
#
# This file is the single source of truth. It is consumed by
# scripts/test-layer.sh (the plain-cargo runner) and, via
# scripts/gen-nextest-groups.sh, by .config/nextest.toml (the nextest runner).
# tests/test_groups.rs fails if the two ever disagree, if a listed binary does not
# exist, or if a binary is listed twice — the exact drift that left
# .config/nextest.toml's `heavy` and `heap` groups empty for their whole life.
#
# Format: <group> <binary>   — one per line, `#` starts a comment.
#
#   heavy — builds git fixture repos or worktrees, or measures wall-clock render
#           budgets. Running two at once starves the timing assertions and
#           multiplies peak RSS.
#   heap  — builds large in-memory indexes.

# Binaries that build git fixture repos, worktrees, or measure wall-clock
# render budgets.
heavy tui_navigation
heavy tui_perf
heavy visual_layout_check
heavy run_lifecycle
heavy pipeline_guards
heavy kb_pipeline
heavy runtime_benchmarks
heavy worktree_policy
heavy diff_scope
heavy sandbox_teardown
heavy acp_server
heavy serve_protocol
heavy planner_coder_branch
heavy resume_cli
heavy hooks_lifecycle
heavy agent_runtime

# Binaries that build large in-memory indexes.
heap structural_index
heap kb_store
heap history_cache
heap repo_intel
